 of a large company wants to conduct a survey to estimate the difference in the proportion of employees from two departments who work overtime at least once a month. The summary statistics for samples from each department are given in the table below, where $n$ is the sample size and $p_{i}$ is the proportion of employees in Department $i$ who work overtime at least once a month.\n\n|  | Department 1 | Department 2 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $n$ | $32$ | $50$ |\n| $p^(^)$ | $0.625$ | $0.7$ |\n\nFind a $99%$ confidence interval for the difference $p_{1} - p_{2}$ between the corresponding population proportions.\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $Z∼N(0, 1)$, the table below shows the $z$-scores $z_{p}$ such that $P(Z > z_{p}) = p$ for some particular values of $p$.*\n\n| $p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $z_{p}$ | $1.282$ | $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |\n\nThe required confidence interval is\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$$,\n{{field-2}}\n$)$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204361 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186201233} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186201234} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186201235} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186201236} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186201237}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186201232}] :question/math-academy-id "q-226131" :question/problem "A district superintendent wants to estimate the difference in the proportion of first-grade and second-grade students participating in after-school sports programs. They conduct two simple random samples of students in their district. The summary statistics of the two samples are given in the table below.\n\n|  | First Grade | Second Grade |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Students | $60$ | $120$ |\n| Students who play sports | $31$ | $86$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The end-points of the $90%$ confidence interval for the difference between the population proportions are approximately $-0.2 ± 0.09$.\n2. All values contained within the $90%$ confidence interval are negative.\n3. The confidence interval data suggests that $p_{1} < p_{2}$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z > 1.645) = 0.05$, where $Z∼N(0, 1)$.* Assume that $p_{1}$ and $p_{2}$ correspond to the first-grade and second-grade students, respectively.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."}] :knowledge-point/title "Applications of Confidence Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048955 :topic/math-academy-id 4943 :topic/title "Confidence Intervals for Two Proportions"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204000 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4 ± 0.592" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200798} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.6 ± 0.820" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200799} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4 ± 0.681" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200800} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.6 ± 0.318" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200801} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4 ± 0.082" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200802}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200797}] :question/math-academy-id "q-223785" :question/problem "![](images/c0/c034e00dbb3aa12894b44c444a843b92fc831a3410186968d9b1005b