he fact that $P(T > 1.66) = 0.05$, where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $80$ degrees of freedom.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Confidence Intervals for Two Means" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050435 :topic/math-academy-id 4946 :topic/title "Confidence Intervals for Two Means: Equal and Unknown Population Variance"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204001 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200810} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200811} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200812} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200813} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200814}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200809}] :question/math-academy-id "q-223787" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d998b155d5639ae5993430e317ad725e15a0fda27da9bd1efa3e5678d6aa27cb.png)\n\nThe scores of two particular geometry and algebra tests are known to be normally distributed with equal variance.\n\nA teacher suspects that the average grade in the geometry test is higher than the average grade in the algebra test. So, they independently and randomly sampled $n_{1} = 15$ students who took the geometry test and $n_{2} = 20$ students who took the algebra test, finding that their mean scores are $x^(―)_{1} = 76$ points and $x^(―)_{2} = 70$ points, respectively, and the pooled variance is $s_{p}^{2} = 4^{2}$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The end-points of the $98%$ confidence interval for the difference between the average scores are approximately $6 ± 3.334$.\n2. All values contained within the $98%$ confidence interval are larger than $3$.\n3. The confidence interval data suggests the geometry mean score is at least $3$ points higher than the algebra mean score.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T > 2.44) = 0.01$, where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $33$ degrees of freedom, as shown in the diagram above.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204330 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200840} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200841} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200842} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200843} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200844}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200839}] :question/math-academy-id "q-224346" :question/problem "![](images/f9/f9448614876f83aff8a755a95dcd76323efefc50b516b2c9142e29d57c30f203.png)\n\nThe diameters of balls for bearings produced by machines X and Y are known to be normally distributed with equal variance. Engineers want to verify the claim that the average diameter of balls produced by machine X is not equal to the average diameter of balls produced by machine Y.\n\nThey independently and randomly sampled $n_{1} = 22$ balls produced by machine X and $n_{2} = 20$ balls produced by machine Y, finding that their mean diameters are $x^(―)_{1} = 20.09$ millimeters and $x^(―)_{2} = 19.85$ millimeters, respectively, and the pooled variance is $s_{p}^{2} = 0.1^{2}$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The end-points of the $96%$ confidence interval for the difference between the average diameters are approximately $0.24 ± 0.065$.\n2. The $96%$ confidence interval does not contain $0$.\n3. The confidence interval data suggests the mean diameter of balls produced by machine X is not equal to the mean diameter of balls produced by machine Y.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T > 2.12) = 0.02$, where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $40$ degrees of freedom, as shown in the diagram above.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Confidence Intervals for Two Means: Applications" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050435 :topic/math-academy-id 4946 :topic/title "Confidence Intervals for Two Means: Equal and Unknown Population Variance"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204002 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204482 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202858} {:answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202859}] :question/math-academy-id "q-253581" :question/problem "Consider the recurrence relation\n$a_{n} = 3a_{n - 1} - 2^{n}, n \\ge 2$.\nThe general solution to this relation for $n \\ge 1$ is$a_{n} = A \\cdot ($ {{field-1}} $)^{n} + ($ {{field-2}} $)$, where $A$ is a constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204483 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_{n}^{(p)} =-3 \\cdot 3^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202861} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_{n}^{(p)} =-5 \\cdot 5^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202862} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_{n}^{(p)} =-3 \\cdot 5^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202863} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_{n}^{(p)} =-5 \\cdot 2^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202864} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_{n}^{(p)} =-5 \\cdot 3^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202865}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202860}] :question/math-academy-id "q-253598" :question/problem "Consider the recurrence relation\n$a_{n} = 2a_{n - 1} - 3 \\cdot 5^{n}, n \\ge 2$.\nGiven that the associated homogeneous recurrence relation has the general solution\n$a_{n}^{(h)} = A \\cdot 2^{n}, n \\ge 1$\nfind the particular solution $a_{n}^{(p)}$ of the inhomogeneous equation."}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Recurrence Relations With Exponential Forcing" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048544 :topic/math-academy-id 5375 :topic/title "First-Order Recurrence Relations With Exponential Forcing"}]}]}
